{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/860307-role-playing-regaining-humanity","id":860307,"title":"Role Playing regaining Humanity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-06T08:05:02-07:00","id":860307,"title":"Role Playing regaining Humanity","content":"So What actions would require for a player to regain humanity? What does it look like for vampire to try to reconnect?<br /> And what could trigger that. Especially for lower humanity vamps?<br /> <br /> A memory? Deja vu? Ziet Geist?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T09:01:39-07:00","id":860353,"title":"","content":"A great start would be trying to reconnect with a detached touchstone, or trying to form an attachment with a new one. Making the effort to contact a formerly dear mortal friend, or maybe their descendants, taking a trip to revisit your place of death or gravestone, looking through old photo albums of your mortal family, spending a night at your old favorite bar under blush of life without feeding, digging your childhood baseball glove out of storage, stuff like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T09:52:05-07:00","id":860384,"title":"","content":"All good examples. I would add things like. Volunteering at a hospital or homeless shelter. Helping people in need. ( instead of harming them )<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T10:54:00-07:00","id":860431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/860307-role-playing-regaining-humanity?p=860384#post860384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All good examples. I would add things like. Volunteering at a hospital or homeless shelter. Helping people in need. ( instead of harming them )</div> </div> </div> </div>Better yet, what about <i>checking into</i> a homeless shelter or long-term care facility? I think actually putting one's self in a vulnerable, human position would do more to help establish empathy for humans than being in a different sort of position of power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T11:08:05-07:00","id":860438,"title":"","content":"This is a good question for someone that DID regain my humanity. Though I kind of cheated by having two touchstones. My ST made me have 2 experience points to regain that Humanity (pretty simple) BUT I had to justify that reason somehow. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2283_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2283\" data-vbnamecard=\"2283\">andreamus</a> brought up using a Touchstone or a memory. Though my ST does not recommend going back to the place of your death. This would probably lower your humanity because it would remind you that you died. What I did was a little creepy though and I also don't recommend it... Basically watching over your Touchstone(s) while they are asleep and reminiscing about what could happen if all of you were human. The thought that their innocence could be swept away just like yours when you were a human and that you probably wouldn't want that innocence to go away (especially if you decide you want to turn them). This is very weak but this is a good start as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11528-dangerus-muyoko-project","name":"Dangerus-Muyoko-Project","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T11:09:42-07:00","id":860439,"title":"","content":"I had a character in my last game who would occasionally skip out on the All Night's Society, go to the mall and hang around humans, get a girlfriend. There's a lot of shows where a vampire or other supernatural regains their humanity by teaming up with or posing as a detective to solve crimes. The idea being that in a police procedural you do a lot of talking with other people and trying to see how someone commit the crime, and why.<br /> <br /> In the comic Vision, out right now, there is a robot that is ostensibly trying to be 'normal' person. He's done this by creating a wife and two robot children, moving them into suburbia and forcing them to live out his idea of a normal life, with the children going to school and the wife doing housework while he goes out and superheroes. I could easily see a vampire doing something similar, using dominate or other powers to usurp a normal family. It's not the sort of thing that can last forever, but it's certainly the kind of thing that can last long enough to fail and, in doing so, perhaps give you some realizations about and appreciation for humanity. And the best thing is it offers so many plot hooks you could put it in a tackle box.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T12:52:38-07:00","id":860493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/860307-role-playing-regaining-humanity?p=860431#post860431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Better yet, what about <i>checking into</i> a homeless shelter or long-term care facility? I think actually putting one's self in a vulnerable, human position would do more to help establish empathy for humans than being in a different sort of position of power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't knew homeless shelters naturally blocked out daylight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T13:07:41-07:00","id":860514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/860307-role-playing-regaining-humanity?p=860493#post860493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't knew homeless shelters naturally blocked out daylight.</div> </div> </div> </div>So go at night?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T15:09:18-07:00","id":860574,"title":"","content":"I'd like to add, that raising humanity, while a desirable thing, does NOT neccessisarily have to be pleasant for the charachter, and might entail things where he forces himself to go through something.<br /> <br /> Note on Buffy the Vampire slayer, the 2nd to last episode of the 2nd season, when angel got his soul back he was a WRECK <br /> <br /> A vampire who regains humanity will probaly often be the same way.<br /> <br /> One more idea, force yourself to do things like go to partys and such... <br /> <br /> one problem? If your humanitys at 1 or 2, getting it back up may be VERY difficult as your social penaltys are very high, so how in that case to have &quot;Meaningful interaction&quot; (essential for pumping humanity back up)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T15:18:00-07:00","id":860583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/860307-role-playing-regaining-humanity?p=860574#post860574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">one problem? If your humanitys at 1 or 2, getting it back up may be VERY difficult as your social penaltys are very high, so how in that case to have &quot;Meaningful interaction&quot; (essential for pumping humanity back up)</div> </div> </div> </div>While I think socializing is going to be hard, it would probably be easier because there's less about the Humanity experience to really get you. It's like the Frankenstein's monster and the blind man thing, or the little girl. It might take a simpler experience than a vampire who's slightly jaded trying to become slightly less jaded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T15:19:23-07:00","id":860584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/860307-role-playing-regaining-humanity?p=860431#post860431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Better yet, what about <i>checking into</i> a homeless shelter or long-term care facility? I think actually putting one's self in a vulnerable, human position would do more to help establish empathy for humans than being in a different sort of position of power.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://kpbs.media.clients.ellingtoncms.com/img/photos/2010/12/08/Picture_tx700.jpg?8e0a8887e886a6ff6e13ee030987b3616fc57cd3\" target=\"_blank\">Sure looks like a non-suicidal idea to me</a>. After all, homeless shelters are known for their tightly sealed single-bed suites and sturdy door locks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T16:09:32-07:00","id":860621,"title":"","content":"Hey, Mahasamatman, this is like the third post in which you're basically repeating my points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T16:49:43-07:00","id":860637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/860307-role-playing-regaining-humanity?p=860584#post860584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://kpbs.media.clients.ellingtoncms.com/img/photos/2010/12/08/Picture_tx700.jpg?8e0a8887e886a6ff6e13ee030987b3616fc57cd3\" target=\"_blank\">Sure looks like a non-suicidal idea to me</a>. After all, homeless shelters are known for their tightly sealed single-bed suites and sturdy door locks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again. Go at night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T18:03:03-07:00","id":860679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/860307-role-playing-regaining-humanity?p=860431#post860431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Better yet, what about <i>checking into</i> a homeless shelter or long-term care facility? I think actually putting one's self in a vulnerable, human position would do more to help establish empathy for humans than being in a different sort of position of power.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like that too. That's a great idea.<br /> <br /> As for the homeless shelter idea. You can definitely go at night. I dont see why we are arguing about this.<br /> <br /> what if you're in Alaska or Minnesota where in the winter it gets dark at 3 in the afternoon... you could still hit the tail end of &quot;normal&quot; business hours.<br /> Even a soup kitchen and serve dinner. Or a night shift guy who does the laundry or helps tuck everyone in and do bed checks... whatever. There are tons of scenarios where that works out just fine. No need to shoot it down because of daylight restrictions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T23:51:39-07:00","id":860831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/860307-role-playing-regaining-humanity?p=860637#post860637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again. Go at night.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the point of comming to a homeless shelter for one night? How does that reconnect you with humanity? That's like a billionaire eating in McDonalds once and then talking about their deep understanding of poor people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T00:22:38-07:00","id":860841,"title":"","content":"Go for...multiple nights?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T00:24:46-07:00","id":860843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/860307-role-playing-regaining-humanity?p=860831#post860831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the point of comming to a homeless shelter for one night? How does that reconnect you with humanity? That's like a billionaire eating in McDonalds once and then talking about their deep understanding of poor people.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm pretty sure that Charlaquin meant &quot;go at night, for several nights&quot;. Spend less time with your coterie and/or Covenant if deemed necessary, don't neglect your other Touchstones, feed somewhere else before entering, that's the gist of it. But volunteering is only the start. You have to reach out to others and really listen to their stories, while being careful with what you reveal about yours.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ninja'd by Enokh. Charlaquin is free to correct me if she wishes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T03:41:54-07:00","id":860918,"title":"","content":"&lt;&lt; How does that reconnect you with humanity? That's like a billionaire eating in McDonalds once and then talking about their deep understanding of poor people. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> Because they're spending their time to (hopefully) develop an empathy toward a segment of humanity who are all linked to each other by a specific event or series of events instead of simply using and discarding humans. Said vampire is likely to notice a few of the same recurring scenarios leading to said misfortune and may or may not decide to use their abilities and resources to ameliorate that specific problem.<br /> It doesn't necessarily have to be living among the homeless or poor, that's just the easiest. It would be just as valid a tactic by choosing to interact regularly on a personal level with people working at a law firm, a hospice, on a college campus, on base housing for military families etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T03:55:03-07:00","id":860925,"title":"","content":"This whole shelter talk reminds me of Fight Club, and how the protagonist tried to fight his insomnia by joining various circles of suffering people to feel more alive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T05:43:00-07:00","id":860989,"title":"","content":"Or how in Mr Smith, the titular character, a retired serial killer goes to AA meetings in order to keep his murderous tendencies in check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T07:21:13-07:00","id":861021,"title":"","content":"So, I hope this doesn't derail anything, but, is this actually a common thing in games? I have run Vampire games since I got Quickstart rules for Masquerade in an Inquest Magazine sometime in the nineties, and in all that time, I have literally <i>never</i> seen anyone buy Humanity. Ever. Everyone I've played with has universally agreed that it a waste of XP. You're probably just going to lose it again anyway--it's better to just fall until your typical actions no longer trigger Humanity loss and stabilize. Unless you're a serial diablerist or mass torture/rape/murder proponent, you will eventually stabilize.<br /> <br /> Hell, when I play, I'm even always that atypical vampire desperately clinging to humanity, trying to actually stay a (relatively) good person, but even I wouldn't waste XP on something that can just go away again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T07:25:55-07:00","id":861024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/860307-role-playing-regaining-humanity?p=861021#post861021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I hope this doesn't derail anything, but, is this actually a common thing in games? I have run Vampire games since I got Quickstart rules for Masquerade in an Inquest Magazine sometime in the nineties, and in all that time, I have literally <i>never</i> seen anyone buy Humanity. Ever. Everyone I've played with has universally agreed that it a waste of XP. You're probably just going to lose it again anyway--it's better to just fall until your typical actions no longer trigger Humanity loss and stabilize. Unless you're a serial diablerist or mass torture/rape/murder proponent, you will eventually stabilize.<br /> <br /> Hell, when I play, I'm even always that atypical vampire desperately clinging to humanity, trying to actually stay a (relatively) good person, but even I wouldn't waste XP on something that can just go away again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't seen anyone spend experiences to increase Humanity in my games, no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T07:37:09-07:00","id":861028,"title":"","content":"I run an atypical group and play atypical characters, so I usually sink XP on Morality-equivalents to try and go above 7. I have a couple of players that do the same, or similar things.<br /> <br /> I also tend to be extra-generous with XP and encourage my players to splurge, buying things they ordinarily wouldn't. I find that it makes such purchases a lot more palatable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T07:52:17-07:00","id":861041,"title":"","content":"It's not uncommon in games I've played or run, but unless the ST incorporates elements to make high Humanity a trait worth keeping, (High humanity vampires could exorcise spirits sent by werewolves. In another setting, low Humanity vampires attracted VII 'recruiters' while high Humanity vampires were resistant or immune to VII possession and sorcery.) generally the consensus is to let it drop to 3 because it's an XP sink and the low Humanity penalties can be easily offset with situational modifiers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 04-08-2016, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T07:57:25-07:00","id":861044,"title":"","content":"I think having rewards for keeping Humanity high and dangers for having Humanity low is an important part of making the stat feel like it actually matters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T08:01:30-07:00","id":861049,"title":"","content":"I have actually. In the game I am currently playing I have had to buy back 3... but it was mostly trying to keep me level at humanity 5. I didnt want to drop anymore... so I would drop to 4 and try all sorts of things to reconnect.. get the ok.. then end up dropping again.. Vicious circle when you are a serial diablerist...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T08:15:54-07:00","id":861057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/860307-role-playing-regaining-humanity?p=860831#post860831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the point of comming to a homeless shelter for one night? How does that reconnect you with humanity? That's like a billionaire eating in McDonalds once and then talking about their deep understanding of poor people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was about to say exactly the same thing. The homeless shelter idea works really well back in first edition when Humanity was a measure of empathy and &quot;goodness.&quot; We have the new system the way I would role play Humanity gain would fit more with how Prince Maxwell of Chicago keeps &quot;in touch&quot; with his city. Going to classes, interacting with Mortals and in general spending several nights just being one of the Sheep.<br /> <br /> Reminding yourself that this is where you came from and without them you couldn't exist as you do now.<br /> <br /> For neonates it could be as simple as going to a bar with intention of &quot;hanging&quot; rather than feeding. For older vampires it would be a longer process of putting yourself among the Kine and treating them as equals instead of just food. It should be role played is a hard thing to do. That even if you get along with those people the Temptation is always there to be &quot;I like them... I want to eat them. When they got excited just then I could hear the pulse of thier blood... I want it.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T08:41:06-07:00","id":861069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeimosMasque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/860307-role-playing-regaining-humanity?p=861057#post861057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was about to say exactly the same thing. The homeless shelter idea works really well back in first edition when Humanity was a measure of empathy and &quot;goodness.&quot; We have the new system the way I would role play Humanity gain would fit more with how Prince Maxwell of Chicago keeps &quot;in touch&quot; with his city. Going to classes, interacting with Mortals and in general spending several nights just being one of the Sheep.<br /> <br /> Reminding yourself that this is where you came from and without them you couldn't exist as you do now.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point of visiting a homeless shelter (and you wouldn't only do it one night, I'd think that would be obvious) <i>is</i> interacting with mortals and in general spending several nights just being one of the Sheep, reminding yourself that this is where you came from and without them you couldn't exist as you do now.<br /> <br /> It's literally the exact same thing Prince Maxwell does, just with a different part of the city's mortal society.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeimosMasque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/860307-role-playing-regaining-humanity?p=861057#post861057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For neonates it could be as simple as going to a bar with intention of &quot;hanging&quot; rather than feeding. For older vampires it would be a longer process of putting yourself among the Kine and treating them as equals instead of just food. It should be role played is a hard thing to do. That even if you get along with those people the Temptation is always there to be &quot;I like them... I want to eat them. When they got excited just then I could hear the pulse of thier blood... I want it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If you replaced &quot;the bar&quot; with &quot;the shelter&quot; in that paragraph, you'd be describing exactly what I was suggesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T08:45:00-07:00","id":861072,"title":"","content":"Charlaquin wasn't suggesting a vampire have their chauffeur drive past the homeless shelter so the vampire could throw eggs wrapped in five dollar bills at people while laughing at them. Any extended contact with people that isn't overwhelmed by vampirism can probably help regain Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T09:26:16-07:00","id":861096,"title":"","content":"Simple solution. If the homeless shelter doesnt work for <i>you</i>. by all means go to the bar instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T11:18:38-07:00","id":861168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/860307-role-playing-regaining-humanity?p=861096#post861096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simple solution. If the homeless shelter doesnt work for <i>you</i>. by all means go to the bar instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to me to getting into the pulse of Humanity. What feels like to be one of those people. No one night would not do. It could a going to the shelter. Hanging out at a drum circle. The people watching at the free concert at the park. Anywhere people are connecting with each other. Then go from watching to trying to interact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/860307-role-playing-regaining-humanity?p=861021#post861021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I hope this doesn't derail anything, but, is this actually a common thing in games? I have run Vampire games since I got Quickstart rules for Masquerade in an Inquest Magazine sometime in the nineties, and in all that time, I have literally <i>never</i> seen anyone buy Humanity. Ever. Everyone I've played with has universally agreed that it a waste of XP. You're probably just going to lose it again anyway--it's better to just fall until your typical actions no longer trigger Humanity loss and stabilize. Unless you're a serial diablerist or mass torture/rape/murder proponent, you will eventually stabilize.<br /> <br /> Hell, when I play, I'm even always that atypical vampire desperately clinging to humanity, trying to actually stay a (relatively) good person, but even I wouldn't waste XP on something that can just go away again.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a style of play. One of many. Not every player will go for it. <br /> But then again you use Humanity different than I. Your table, your rules.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T15:19:24-07:00","id":861366,"title":"","content":"Here's an idea: instead of spending Experiences to raise Humanity, you can do it through role-play in a manner that is most eye-opening for your PC. Homeless shelters, college campuses, the retro arcade down the block that's getting surprisingly popular with the new generation, you name it. When you and the ST agree you've significantly improved your connection with what you used to be, a dot of Humanity is regained. This can take as long as you deem necessary, but I imagine most would settle for something between several scenes and a chapter (which can consist of multiple game sessions).<br /> <br /> However, if you choose to go further and risk your goals in the Danse Macabre, whatever they are, the Experiences you would have spent to increase your Humanity are actually gained. Combined with the Experiences received through Conditions, Dramatic Failures, Aspirations and so on, you should have a good amount to spend on Merits that require high Humanity. These Merits should have significant benefits, which could include dice bonuses and dice tricks to resist Frenzy/Ride The Wave, greater protection against mind control (even from non-vampiric sources) and assorted advantages over the Strix and other abominations related to vampires.<br /> <br /> That lets you reach high Humanity <i>and</i> have enough Experiences left to raise other traits. Sanctity Of Merits would still apply, but this whole process should not be superficial or safe.<br /> <br /> How does that sound?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T18:43:52-07:00","id":861507,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't mind exorcising &quot;spend XP to regain Humanity&quot;, and instead making the Humanity regain a reward for fulfilling an (or a chain of) Aspiration(s) directly focused on Humanity. But on the other hand, I really dislike XP as a thing and prefer mile stones advancements and just communicating what players want to grow and then well, this thing growing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T18:58:23-07:00","id":861513,"title":"","content":"I have really enjoyed the fact that each 2e Integrity Anologue has its own means of increasing. My favorites are the ones that are increased without experience - Harmony breaking both directions and Clarity being a reward for resolving the Accuity Condition are both perfect ways to mechanically show what those traits represent in the narrative of their respective gamelines. Demons being able to have multiple Covers is similarly awesome, and while Cover can be bought with normal experiences, Cover Experiences are a good way to show how Cover is increased. I haven't read Beast, but using Satiety as a resource sounds like a really cool idea. Humanity is cool in that it retains the 1e idea of Breaking Points as hierarchal, with lower-Humanity characters being too jaded to even be affected by the higher up ones. But it is kind of a shame that it's regained the same way Integrity is. A Humanity Beat system would be a decent way to address that. Honestly, I almost think it would be more appropriate to Vampire's themes if Humanity, once lost, was gone for good. But going that route would cut off some of the cool ideas people have given here for how Humanity might be regained.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T19:25:33-07:00","id":861532,"title":"","content":"It would also make it impossible to get more than 7 dots of Humanity, which makes one of the most fun things to play in Vampire (high Humanity vamps) a non-viable thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T22:58:20-07:00","id":861615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/860307-role-playing-regaining-humanity?p=861168#post861168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then again you use Humanity different than I. Your table, your rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I do a lot of things differently, but I really don't think I use Humanity any differently.<br /> <br /> But yes, I think Vampires should be able to get Humanity back without XP. Not sure how to handle it, exactly, but yes, I approve of that idea. I already don't let people buy Blood Potency with XP--I raise the PC's blood potencies automatically when they hit certain XP thresh holds. Humanity wouldn't be able to work like that, though. I guess Humanity specific beats would be best, but, that would be hard to adjudicate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T08:17:02-07:00","id":863158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/860307-role-playing-regaining-humanity?p=861513#post861513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Humanity Beat system would be a decent way to address that. Honestly, I almost think it would be more appropriate to Vampire's themes if Humanity, once lost, was gone for good. But going that route would cut off some of the cool ideas people have given here for how Humanity might be regained.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm working on a Samurai Fantasy conversion for my group, as we want to experiment with one of our favorite worlds using CofD, and I'm using Honor as a Samurai's Integrity analogue. One of features I included in it is ability to reduce your possible maximum Honor permanently in exchange for declaring that specific actions do not force Honor Checks anymore. I think you could use this idea to enhance themes you mentioned in Vampire, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}